  "meaning": "A bounded-preview instrument pairs a visibly turned, deep ivory-faced source-document assembly with a smaller matching ivory layout inside a thick machined aperture housing. Each stands on a low mounting plate with rounded plan corners, crisp edge breaks and recessed screws; the entire left assembly, including its columns and base, is rotated relative to the right assembly. Two open alignment rails, a copper dimension stop, a screw-driven preview carriage, calibration ticks, retained corner screws, and supporting shoes make the source-to-preview relationship explicit. Detailed machined construction, actual recessed marks, separate fasteners, brushed polished steel, dark red-brown granular corrosion islands with broken oxide rims, pitted normal relief and dull oxidized metal between crusts, graphite interiors, directional softbox reflections, and genuine transparent negative space.",
